    "roles": ["band_member", "session", "composer"],
    "summary": "The Red Hot Chili Peppers' drummer from December 1988, the last to audition, who looked 'very Detroit and rock' and played like it. A Bonham fan from Michigan whom a percussionist, Larry Fratangelo, turned to funk: a rock drummer's power under a funk drummer's hands, ghost notes whispered round a hard backbeat, the hats with the quarters leaned on, and a fast right foot locked to Flea. Higher Ground's eighths on the kick, Give It Away's rimshots, Under the Bridge's cross-stick, Can't Stop's ghosts, Dark Necessities' sixteenths. 'I steal loads of stuff. So go ahead and steal from me.'"
  },
